  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I originally observed this problem in the 1097 Vive Focus build of VRChat. It got fixed with the viveport release of 1102, but now it's back again.\nMirrors are turned into an eye-splitting mess, and the FOV is very strange making everything look small. Stretching my arms out in full, it feels like they only go half the way. Looking down at my feet also seem like I'm much tinier than I should be.\nSeems like this build runs somewhat faster, so I wonder if this is related using not/using il2cpp? The 1102 build was kinda sluggish at times, but it didn't have this issue. Not able to confirm because I do not know a way to downgrade on the Vive Focus Plus and I have no backups of the old client version even if I knew how to do it.\nAlso is there any way I can get logs out of the android version?\nScreenshots showing the exact version as reported in the menu, as well as the broken mirror. (The FOV issues are not noticeable in the screenshots, only in person). Interestingly the camera for the gallery and the icon do not seem to have the broken mirror issue.",
